  "user_request_original": "Using Transfer Matrix Method, optimize a 22-layer dielectric stack on CaF2 substrate with air incidence at normal angle. Layer sequence: Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS, Ge, ZnS. Initialize all thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness at 3300 nm center wavelength. Set thickness optimization bounds [100, 500] nm for all layers. Evaluate transmittance across four bands: 2500-3100 nm (suppress), 3250-3350 nm (transmit), 4200-4300 nm (transmit), 4450-5000 nm (suppress). Use Ge and ZnS as dielectric materials with CaF2 substrate. No metal layers allowed. Total layer count fixed at 22. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
